nment":"destination","family":"destination","romance":"primary","ski":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC","bundle"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"The Lake Placid village + lodge table","status":"future","tier":"comfort","price_band":"~USD 40-250/pp","timing":"standing; strongest ski + summer/foliage","draw_rank":1,"hook":"Main Street restaurants above Mirror Lake, the lodge kitchens and Adirondack producers — a compact, walkable food scene as the après-and-evening layer","si":"culinary","blurb":"Main Street restaurants above Mirror Lake, the lodge kitchens and Adirondack producers — a compact, walkable food scene as the après-and-evening layer","when":"standing; strongest ski + summer/foliage","commission":"bundle/hotel on stay","wells":["stay","eat"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culinary","ski"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"primary","entertainment":"destination","family":"destination","romance":"destination","ski":"evidenced","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["bundle","hotel"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"When is the best time to visit Lake Placid / Whiteface?","a":"**Passes — NOT Ikon:** Whiteface is on ORDA''s **SKI3** season pass (with Gore and Belleayre) and joined the **Mountain Collective** for 2025/26 (up to two days) — it is **not on the Ikon Pass.**","source":"https://orda.org/2025/07/22/whiteface-mountain-joins-mountain-collective-pass-roster-for-2025-2026-season/","accessed":"2026-07-13"},{"q":"How do I get to Lake Placid / Whiteface?","a":"**Whiteface — the biggest vertical in the East:** the greatest continuous vertical drop in eastern North America, ~3,430 ft (incl. the hike-to Slides); ~94 trails over ~299 acres, 12 lifts, ~99% snowmaking; the 1980 Olympic alpine venue, ORDA-operated.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whiteface_Mountain","accessed":"2026-07-13"},{"q":"What is worth doing in Lake Placid / Whiteface?","a":"**Ride the Olympic bobsled track at Mt. Van Hoevenberg** — a passenger bobsled run with a pro pilot down the descendant of the 1930 Olympic track — TIMING: winter sliding; verify ORDA calendar — **PRICE TIER `[premier]`** — COMMISSION: DMC/affiliate (some pass-through)","source":"https://mtvanhoevenberg.com/","accessed":"2026-07-13"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Lake Placid & Whiteface Ski Guide: America''s Two-Time Olympic Town & the Biggest Vertical in the East","meta_description":"Plan Lake Placid, New York — the only US town to host the Winter Olympics twice (1932 + 1980) — and Whiteface, the biggest ski vertical in the East (~3,430 ft, the 1980 Olympic downhill venue, ORDA-run). Ride the Olympic bobsled track, skate the Herb Brooks Arena, stay at Lake Placid Lodge, with real timing, cold/ice/winter-driving safety and booking intel.","slug":"lake-placid-whiteface-new-york","primary_keyword":"Lake Placid Whiteface ski guide","long_tail":["Whiteface Mountain biggest vertical east","Lake Placid 1932 1980 Winter Olympics","Mt Van Hoevenberg bobsled ride","Herb Brooks Arena Miracle on Ice","Lake Placid Lodge Relais Chateaux"],"search_language":"es-US","local_keywords":["esqui en Whiteface Mountain","Lake Placid Juegos Olimpicos de invierno 1932 1980","el mayor desnivel de esqui del este","Milagro sobre hielo Herb Brooks Arena","hoteles de lujo en Lake Placid"],"hreflang":["en","es-US"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-13","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-13","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa","read":"2026-08-20T14:47:42Z","source_updated":"2026-08-18T10:29:04+01:00"}]}},"booking":{"codes":[],"advisory_verified":"2026-07-13","flag":"US-domestic advisory convention — flag for Zero-Drift","note":"US domestic; real risk is Eastern winter (extreme Adirondack cold + wind on Whiteface with upper-mountain wind-holds, ice/hardpack + freeze-thaw, Northeast winter driving), not security","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"ski","status":"future"},{"si":"entertainment","status":"future"},{"si":"ultra","status":"future"},{"si":"family","status":"future"},{"si":"romance","status":"live"},{"si":"culinary","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Lake Placid Lodge — Relais & Chateaux","why_ultra":"Adirondack Great Camp turned Relais & Chateaux landmark on the lakeshore — timber-and-stone rooms + lakefront cabins, celebrated table + wine cellar, High Peaks views; the ultra anchor of the region","earning":"consortia/luxury on application","virtuoso_value_add":true,"mor":"commissionable-rack","tier":"luxury","price_band":"~USD 650-1,500+/night (peak far higher)"},{"name":"The Whiteface Lodge (Lake Placid)","why_ultra":"Gilded-Age-Great-Camp-style luxury resort in the High Peaks woodlands — all-suite timber lodging, Conde Nast top-100 spa, pools + full resort service","earning":"consortia/property on application","virtuoso_value_add":true,"mor":"commissionable-rack","tier":"luxury","price_band":"~USD 500-1,000+/night peak"},{"name":"Private Adirondack lakefront camp + guide + chef (Lake Placid)","why_ultra":"exclusive-use luxury ''camp'' on Lake Placid — private ski guide, in-home chef, boat + concierge, plus arranged Olympic-venue experiences","earning":"property managers + guide/DMC","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"~USD 1,500-10,000+/night whole-home lakefront peak"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-13","hero":{"query":"Lake Placid / Whiteface, United States"},"geo":{"lat":44.2795,"lng":-73.9799},"orbit":[],"orbit_country":["alta-utah","aspen-snowmass-colorado","beaver-creek-colorado","big-sky-montana","breckenridge-colorado","copper-mountain-colorado","crested-butte-colorado","crystal-mountain-washington","deer-valley-utah","heavenly-california","jackson-hole-wyoming","keystone-colorado","killington-vermont","mammoth-california","mt-bachelor-oregon","mt-baker-washington","mt-hood-meadows-oregon","northstar-tahoe-california","palisades-tahoe-california","park-city-utah","snowbird-utah","soldier-hollow-utah","steamboat-colorado","stevens-pass-washington","stowe-vermont","sugarbush-mad-river-glen-vermont","summit-at-snoqualmie-washington","sunday-river-sugarloaf-maine","telluride-colorado","timberline-mt-hood-oregon","vail-colorado","white-mountains-new-hampshire","winter-park-colorado"]}'::jsonb, 13),
  ('mammoth-california', '12A', 'Mammoth Mountain', 'United States', 'California''s highest mountain, deepest snow, and longest season', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Pacific Coast', '{"adventure","culinary","entertainment","expedition","family","romance","ski","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Mammoth = Alterra / Ikon (Alterra HQ Denver); CALIFORNIA''S HIGHEST ski resort (summit 11,053 ft, base 7,953 ft, ~3,100 ft vertical; town ~7,880 ft); a VOLCANIC lava-dome complex on the Long Valley Caldera","3,500+ acres, 175-178 trails (15% beg / 48% int / 37% adv), 25 lifts (~59,000/hr); ~400 in snow; no night skiing","ONE OF THE LONGEST SEASONS IN THE US: Nov-May typical, often into June, sometimes July - regularly the last major US resort open; distinctive long-spring demand window","Alterra also owns June Mountain (~1,500 ac, 41 trails, family-oriented) ~20+ mi N near June Lake","GENUINE natural hot springs in the Eastern Sierra (a real, rare ski-trip amenity): Benton Hot Springs confirmed (~135F source); Long Valley/Crowley springs widely known - Wellness is LIVE via the natural springs, NOT a hotel-spa claim","US-TRAFFIC CANDOR: among CA''s biggest/most-visited but no per-resort count published - consensus only","Long haul: LA ~5 hr / Reno ~3 hr via US-395; Mammoth Yosemite Airport (MMH) ~7 mi E seasonal winter flights (weather-unreliable); TIOGA PASS (SR-120) CLOSED in winter -> Bay Area detour","NO on-site cat/heli (lift-served; regional guided touring only); VOLCANIC CO2 hazard near Horseshoe Lake; Hot Creek soaking PROHIBITED (dangerous geothermal); Ikon/lift prices dynamic"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police/fire/medical/rescue dispatch); alert ski patrol on-mountain","hospital":"Mammoth Hospital, Mammoth Lakes - small critical-access hospital, 24/7 ER (site 403''d - verify); larger Northern Inyo Hospital in Bishop (~40 mi S)","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"ALTITUDE (base ~7,953 ft GENUINELY HIGH, summit ~11,053 ft; SoCal drive market arrives sea-level - hydrate, ease alcohol, descend if AMS worsens); VOLCANIC CO2 (Horseshoe Lake ~170-ac tree-kill zone can hold lethal CO2 in depressions/snow-wells/cabins - avoid low pockets, heed signage); AVALANCHE backcountry - Eastern Sierra Avalanche Center (ESAC, esavalanche.org, ''eastside-region'' - VERIFY named sub-zones); beacon/probe/shovel + guide, never duck ropes; tree-wells; US-395 winter driving + Caltrans chains + TIOGA PASS (SR-120) closed all winter; HOT CREEK soaking PROHIBITED (scalding/fluctuating geothermal - use only established safe springs)","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa","read":"2026-09-01T16:18:24Z","page_updated":"2026-08-18T10:29:04+01:00","source_country":"usa","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely"},"timing":{"peak":"High winter (Christmas/NY, MLK, Presidents'' Week/Feb, powder weekends) - heavy SoCal drive-market demand","shoulder":"early season (Nov-mid Dec) + the long spring (Apr-May)","green":"deep summer bike-park/gondola season is its own draw; true lulls are late-spring weekdays + October","booking_lead":"Christmas/NY + Presidents'' + Westin/Village 3-6 mo (holidays longer); regular winter 2-4 mo; SoCal drive market books holidays early","off_season_specials":"long spring skiing; summer bike park + Devils Postpile/Yosemite; festivals; midweek value","event_peaks":"Christmas/NY, MLK + Presidents'', spring break; summer festivals (chamber music, reggae - verify dates)","fire_date":"FIRE spring early-bird (Apr-Jun) Ikon renewals + long-spring push; fire winter again Sep-Nov"},"jewels":[{"name":"Ski California''s highest mountain","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"window dynamic; package best value","timing":"ski Nov-Jun","draw_rank":1,"hook":"an 11,053-ft summit over 3,500+ acres of o